rows.answer:
Under APP 11.2, if certain conditions are met, an APP entity must take reasonable steps in the circumstances to destroy the personal information or to ensure it is de-identified. These conditions, as set out in APP 11.2(a), APP 11.2(b), APP 11.2(c), and APP 11.2(d), are:
1. The entity holds personal information about an individual;
2. The entity no longer needs that information for any purpose for which it may be used or disclosed under the Schedule;
3. The information is not contained in a Commonwealth record; and
4. The entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the information.

