rows.answer:
Under s 6(1) "agency", "agency" is defined to mean:
- a Minister (s 6(1) "agency" (a));
- a Department (s 6(1) "agency" (b));
- a body (whether incorporated or not), or a tribunal, established or appointed for a public purpose by or under a Commonwealth law, except for an incorporated company, society or association (s 6(1) "agency" (c)(i)) or an organisation registered under the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009 or a branch of such an organisation (s 6(1) "agency" (c)(ii));
- a body (whether incorporated or not), or a tribunal, established for a public purpose by or under a law of a State or Territory as in force in an external Territory (other than a law providing for the incorporation of companies, societies or associations), unless exempted by the Minister under subsection (5A) (s 6(1) "agency" (ca));
- a body established or appointed by the Governor-General, or by a Minister, otherwise than by or under a Commonwealth law (s 6(1) "agency" (d));
- a person holding or performing the duties of an office established by or under, or an appointment made under, a Commonwealth law, excluding a person who is the Secretary of a Department by virtue of holding that office (s 6(1) "agency" (e));
- a person holding or performing the duties of an office established by or under, or an appointment made under, a law of a State or Territory as in force in an external Territory, unless exempted by the Minister under subsection (5A) (s 6(1) "agency" (ea));
- a person holding or performing the duties of an appointment made by the Governor-General, or by a Minister, otherwise than under a Commonwealth law (s 6(1) "agency" (f));
- a federal court (s 6(1) "agency" (g));
- the Australian Federal Police (s 6(1) "agency" (h));
- a court of Norfolk Island (s 6(1) "agency" (ha));
- an eligible hearing service provider (s 6(1) "agency" (k)); or
- the service operator under the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010 (s 6(1) "agency" (l)).

