rows.answer:
Under the Privacy Act 1988, the definition of an "agency" is not provided in the retrieved clauses. However, a "State or Territory authority" is defined under s 6C(3) as:
- a State or Territory Minister (s 6C(3)(a));
- a Department of State of a State or Territory (s 6C(3)(b));
- a body (whether incorporated or not), or a tribunal, established or appointed for a public purpose by or under a law of a State or Territory, other than: (1) an incorporated company, society or association, or (2) an association of employers or employees registered or recognised under a law of a State or Territory dealing with industrial dispute resolution (s 6C(3)(c), s 6C(3)(c)(i), and s 6C(3)(c)(ii));
- a body established or appointed, otherwise than by or under a law of a State or Territory, by a Governor of a State, the Australian Capital Territory Executive, the Administrator of the Northern Territory, or a State or Territory Minister (s 6C(3)(d), s 6C(3)(d)(i), s 6C(3)(d)(ii), s 6C(3)(d)(iii), and s 6C(3)(d)(v));
- a person holding or performing the duties of an office established by or under, or an appointment made under, a law of a State or Territory, other than the office of head of a State or Territory Department (s 6C(3)(e));
- a person holding or performing the duties of an appointment made, otherwise than under a law of a State or Territory, by a Governor of a State, the Australian Capital Territory Executive, the Administrator of the Northern Territory, or a State or Territory Minister (s 6C(3)(f), s 6C(3)(f)(i), s 6C(3)(f)(ii), s 6C(3)(f)(iii), and s 6C(3)(f)(v)); or
- a State or Territory court (s 6C(3)(g)).

